  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), the MFY Pro handle straight from the pilot's seat: both grip heads, the screen hub in the middle",
  "mappingSource": "MOZA MFY Yoke Handle quick guide p.1 \"Buttons / Switches Description\" (www.gtomega.co.uk/cdn/shop/files/1512135c149fe73ad0fa548b39598aca5429.pdf) names the controls: per grip a tall analog stick with light ring (1 auxiliary axis switch left / 8 POV control axis switch right), a cross-shaped switch below it (3 trim switch left / 10 view switch right), a round button (2 / 9 AP disconnect), PTT buttons and trigger axes on the back. The button numbers are the catalog's (from a local game configuration, not in public documentation); the catalog's \"switch\" vs \"analog hat switch\" names match the cross switch vs the analog stick.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The photo shows the MFY Pro (screen in the hub). The catalog's center buttons HOME/S1/S2/Center/HDG/NAV/ALT/APR belong to the MFY (non-Pro) checklist plate and are not on this photo. The catalog's panel.* parts (NAV/BEACON/STROBE/BATT/FUEL PUMP/PITOT toggles, SYS/ENG, knob, FLAPS, GEAR) are on the yoke base's front panel (seen on the AY210 photos), not on this handle. The quick guide lists two trigger axes (16, rudder/Z + slider) and analog stick axes that the catalog does not have as parts; the paddles behind the grips are those triggers.",
